{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>hairy, and he blessed him.</b> Because he suspected that he might be deserving of a curse, as it says: <b>and I bring upon myself a curse</b>. And so the Sages said: one who suspects his fellow of something in which there is nothing must appease him — and not only that, but he must bless him, as in the case of Eli when he suspected Hannah of drunkenness (I Samuel 1:13–17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Sforno cites the verse phrase וְהֵבֵאתִי עָלַי קְלָלָה from Genesis 27:12 itself (Jacob's words to Rebekah), here applied to Isaac's parallel situation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:00.320339961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}